0-CODE/                              # Public source for Claude Code, Codex and OpenCode.
                                     # Installed framework lives under a project's .0-code/.
|
+-- README.md                        # Overview and public installation source.
+-- README.<language>.md             # Ten translations tracking the English README.
+-- INTEGRATE.md                     # Agent workflow: scan, preview, install, upgrade, remove, start.
+-- QUICKSTART.md                    # Manual workflow and explicit toolset scope selection.
+-- CLAUDE_CODE_SETUP.md              # Native Claude hooks, restart and owner preferences.
+-- GUIDELINE.md                     # Shared cycle and development checks.
+-- CHANGELOG.md                     # Historical changes and their evidence limits.
+-- CONTRIBUTING.md                  # Claims, verification and translation review.
+-- SECURITY.md                      # Ownership, credentials and reporting.
+-- LICENSE                          # MIT.
+-- VERSION                          # Release number source.
|
+-- bootstrap.sh / bootstrap.ps1     # Thin wrappers around tools/0code.mjs install.
+-- provision-toolset.sh / .ps1       # Thin wrappers for independent user tool delivery.
|
+-- core/                            # Shared drivers, gates, guards and installation lifecycle.
|   +-- supervisor.mjs               # External driver for all three engines.
|   +-- project-config.mjs           # Configuration schema, defaults and document roles.
|   +-- project-inventory.mjs        # Read-only project scan; owner tools take precedence.
|   +-- project-installation.mjs     # Owned project install, upgrade and uninstall.
|   +-- project-migration.mjs        # Explicit adoption, relocation and proven 1.x migration.
|   +-- project-adoption.mjs         # Reviewed hashes and retained project extensions.
|   +-- document-relocation.mjs      # Exact document moves and cycle pointer updates.
|   +-- project-doctor.mjs           # Local checks; no model call or proof of live MCP access.
|   +-- project-start.mjs            # Bind a cycle prompt and print driver commands.
|   +-- user-installation.mjs        # Independent user tools and their native settings receipt.
|   +-- installation-transaction.mjs # Preflight, bounded writes, journals and recovery.
|   +-- backends/                    # Claude, Codex and OpenCode adapters and process launch.
|
+-- hooks/                           # Native Claude Stop, guard, transcript and usage hooks.
+-- lib/                             # Atomic state writer, parsers and shared utilities.
+-- tools/                           # Lifecycle CLI, provisioning and public check utilities.
+-- schemas/                         # Configuration and installation receipt schemas.
+-- templates/                       # Cycle, project instructions, settings and audit templates.
+-- commands/                        # Framework commands; excludes private stock command bodies.
+-- skills/orchestrator-wrapper/     # Framework instructions for the current cycle stage.
|
+-- config/                          # Secret-free examples, schemas and settings templates.
|   +-- mcp-manifest.example.json    # Five default local MCP plus optional setup examples.
|   +-- .env.example                 # Environment variable names; no real credentials.
|
+-- toolset/                         # Generated public catalog, definitions only.
|   +-- catalog.json                # context7, playwright, chrome-devtools,
|   |                               # sequential-thinking and memory.
|   +-- CATALOG.md                  # Public boundary and npm prerequisite requirements.
|
+-- docs/                            # Public operation guides and schemas.
|   +-- PROJECT_SETTINGS.md          # One configuration table, including document roles.
|   +-- ENGINE_SETTINGS.md           # Owner model, effort, login, guard and driver settings.
|   +-- PROVEN.md                    # Historical measurements and their limitations.
|   +-- two-modes.md                 # Interactive hook and external supervisor drivers.
|   +-- failure-modes.md             # Failure behavior and investigation guidance.
|   +-- schemas/                    # Cycle artifact contracts.
|
+-- tests/                           # Public unit/integration checks and smoke workflow.
+-- .github/                         # CI and contribution templates.

Public exclusions: private skill, agent, command and rule bodies; personal settings
and credentials; development reports, prompts, decisions, findings and logs;
config/legacy-installations.json and checks requiring its ownership evidence;
the development-only exporter and its private rules. No Claude plugin installation.

New installations default all nine document roles to .0-code/docs/: STATE.md,
ROADMAP.md, reports/, decisions/, todo/, logs/, prompts/, prompts/templates/ and
userdocs/. Explicit external roles remain supported; upgrade keeps existing paths
unless relocation is requested. Cycle documents belong to the project and remain
outside the receipt; they survive upgrade/uninstall. Logs are ignored. Runtime and
backups belong in ignored .0-code/run/ and are removed by uninstall. Reviewed
adopted bin/, claude/ and README extensions remain separate from replaceable code.
